From 61f5723dc5eb0f2d2d4a1786c15caaf8e1c66bab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 02:55:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] d/wmr: Fix freshness check accepting stale samples with
 a negative delta

Found by testing: get_tracked_pose's freshness gate compared
at_timestamp_ns - last_sample_ts against the 200ms threshold directly,
with no lower bound. When the constellation tracker's sample timestamp
(from the camera/blob-observation clock domain) reads ahead of
Monado's own at_timestamp_ns -- observed several seconds ahead in
testing, cause not fully understood, but real and reproducible -- the
delta goes negative and is trivially "less than 200ms", so a single
frozen, no-longer-updating sample kept passing as fresh for 6+ seconds
straight while sample_count stayed flat. Exactly the "stale position
silently marked tracked" failure mode the freshness check was
supposed to prevent in the first place.

Fix: compare the absolute value of the delta. Treats "suspiciously far
in either time direction" as equally stale, which is the conservative
choice until the two clock domains' relationship is actually
understood.
---
 src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_base.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_base.c b/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_base.c
index e015ebc68..56b267295 100644
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_base.c
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_base.c
@@ -640,8 +640,18 @@ wmr_controller_base_get_tracked_pose(struct xrt_device *xdev,
 	// hasn't been seen by a camera recently, e.g. it's out of view or the feature is off -- a stale
 	// position silently marked "tracked" would be worse than the honest placeholder.
 	static const int64_t WMR_CONSTELLATION_MAX_SAMPLE_AGE_NS = 200000000; // 200ms, ~6 frames at 30fps
+	int64_t constellation_sample_age_ns = at_timestamp_ns - wcb->constellation.last_timestamp_ns;
+	if (constellation_sample_age_ns < 0) {
+		constellation_sample_age_ns = -constellation_sample_age_ns;
+	}
+	// Absolute value: the constellation tracker's blob-observation timestamps and Monado's own
+	// at_timestamp_ns aren't guaranteed to be in the same clock domain (observed the sample's
+	// timestamp reading several seconds AHEAD of at_timestamp_ns in testing) -- a plain "is it in the
+	// past and recent" check let a frozen, stale sample pass as fresh for 6+ seconds straight because
+	// the negative delta was trivially less than the threshold. Treat "suspiciously far in either
+	// direction" as equally stale.
 	if (wcb->constellation.tracker != NULL && wcb->constellation.sample_count > 0 &&
-	    at_timestamp_ns - wcb->constellation.last_timestamp_ns < WMR_CONSTELLATION_MAX_SAMPLE_AGE_NS) {
+	    constellation_sample_age_ns < WMR_CONSTELLATION_MAX_SAMPLE_AGE_NS) {
 		pose.position = wcb->constellation.last_pose.position;
 		relation.relation_flags = (enum xrt_space_relation_flags)(
 		    relation.relation_flags | XRT_SPACE_RELATION_POSITION_VALID_BIT |
-- 
2.47.3

